> [!NOTE]
> Stacked on #71823. Only the last commit is new.

In local and `emitDeclarationOnly` compilation, `ngtsc`'s `extractHostDirectives` keeps every `hostDirectives` entry or reports it. An entry that evaluates to a reference is emitted as one. An entry that is still dynamic is emitted verbatim (`WrappedNodeExpr`) when it's written as an identifier or property access, and any other expression reports `NG11003`. Without `emitDeclarationOnly`, the partial evaluator still resolves values across the compilation unit.

`ng-analyze` dropped entries silently instead. An undeclared identifier, a property access on one, or a string disappeared from the emitted metadata. An entry that depended on another file (an imported array, a spread of one, a conditional on an imported flag, or an imported `inputs` mapping) dropped the whole `hostDirectives` field.

This change:
1. Evaluates `hostDirectives` across the compilation unit without `emitDeclarationOnly`. Under `emitDeclarationOnly`, only ambient `.d.ts` globals fold (e.g. `COMPILED ? DirA : DirB`).
2. Emits a still-dynamic entry verbatim when its array element is an identifier or property access, and reports `NG11003` otherwise. An entry flagged as an unsupported expression stays flagged unless it folds to a concrete value, because `ngtsc` re-anchors a dynamic value on the outermost expression it evaluated.
3. Reports `NG1010` for a non-array value or a non-reference entry. An `inputs`/`outputs` value that isn't an array yields no mapping instead of dropping the entry, matching `parseHostDirectivesMapping`.

### Input

```ts
// deps.ts
import {Directive} from '@angular/core';

@Directive({selector: '[depA]'})
export class DepA {}

@Directive({selector: '[depB]'})
export class DepB {}

export const HOST_DIRECTIVES = [DepA, DepB];

// app.ts (compiled with compilationMode: 'experimental-local')
import {Component} from '@angular/core';
import {HOST_DIRECTIVES} from './deps';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  template: '',
  hostDirectives: HOST_DIRECTIVES,
})
export class AppComponent {}
```

### Output Before Fix (`ngp`)

```ts
static ɵcmp = /*@__PURE__*/ i0.ɵɵdefineComponent({
  type: AppComponent,
  selectors: [['app-root']],
  decls: 0,
  vars: 0,
  template: function AppComponent_Template(rf: number, ctx: any): any {},
  encapsulation: 2,
});
```

### Output After Fix (`ngp` — matches `ngtsc`)

```ts
static ɵcmp = /*@__PURE__*/ i0.ɵɵdefineComponent({
  type: AppComponent,
  selectors: [['app-root']],
  features: [i0.ɵɵHostDirectivesFeature([i1.DepA, i1.DepB])],
  decls: 0,
  vars: 0,
  template: function AppComponent_Template(rf: number, ctx: any): any {},
  encapsulation: 2,
});
```

In `ngtsc`'s `StaticInterpreter.resolveForeignFunctionCall` (`visitFfrExpression`), references returned by foreign function resolution have `node.synthetic = true`. Consequently, `createModuleWithProvidersResolver` marks the unwrapped `ngModule` reference as `synthetic = true`, causing `NgModuleDecoratorHandler` to set `remoteScopesMayRequireCycleProtection = true` so remotely-scoped `ɵɵsetComponentScope` calls wrap their dependency arrays in closures.

In `ng-analyze`, `ClassData::to_wire` (`ng-analyze/src/analyzer/class_data.rs`) computes `remote_scopes_may_require_cycle_protection: any_synthetic(&m.declarations) || any_synthetic(&m.imports)`. However, when a function or static method call (such as `AddonModule.forRoot()`) could not be statically evaluated from its body and fell back to `try_foreign_function_call` using its `ModuleWithProviders<T>` return type, `resolve_type` did not call `mark_value_synthetic(...)` and `mark_value_synthetic` lacked an arm for `ResolvedValue::Synthetic(SyntheticValue::ModuleWithProviders { .. })`. Because `ng_module.synthetic` remained `false` (including across Stage 2 cross-file `Incomplete` hole substitution), `remote_scopes_may_require_cycle_protection` stayed `false` and `src/processor.ts` emitted eager array literals in remotely-scoped `ɵɵsetComponentScope` calls instead of wrapping them in closures.

This change wraps the resolved return-type value in `mark_value_synthetic(...)` inside `try_foreign_function_call` and adds a `SyntheticValue::ModuleWithProviders` arm to `mark_value_synthetic`.

### Input

```ts
// addon.ts
import {Directive, ModuleWithProviders, NgModule} from '@angular/core';

@Directive({selector: '[addonDir]', standalone: false})
export class AddonDir {}

@NgModule({declarations: [AddonDir], exports: [AddonDir]})
export class AddonModule {
  static forRoot(): ModuleWithProviders<AddonModule> {
    return (globalThis as any).dynamicMwp;
  }
}

// comp-b.component.ts
import {Component} from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'comp-b',
  template: '<div addonDir>CompB: <comp-a></comp-a></div>',
  standalone: false,
})
export class CompB {}

// app.module.ts
import {Component, NgModule} from '@angular/core';
import {AddonModule} from './addon';
import {CompB} from './comp-b.component';

@NgModule({
  declarations: [CompA, CompB],
  imports: [AddonModule.forRoot()],
  exports: [CompB],
})
export class AppModule {}

@Component({
  selector: 'comp-a',
  template: '<div>CompA: <comp-b></comp-b></div>',
  standalone: false,
})
export class CompA {}
```

### Output Before Fix (`ngp`)

```ts
(() => {
  (typeof ngDevMode === 'undefined' || ngDevMode) &&
    i0.ɵɵsetComponentScope(CompB, [AddonDir, CompA, CompB], []);
})();
```

### Output After Fix (`ngp` — matches `ngtsc`)

```ts
(() => {
  (typeof ngDevMode === 'undefined' || ngDevMode) &&
    i0.ɵɵsetComponentScope(
      CompB,
      function () {
        return [i1.AddonDir, CompA, CompB];
      },
      [],
    );
})();
```

In `ngtsc`'s `NgModuleDecoratorHandler.analyze`, when `declarations` contains an external `.d.ts` class (`NG6001`) or `resolveTypeList` fails (`NG1010`/`NG6005`), `analyze` aborts without producing `analysis` (or throws `FatalDiagnosticError`). Consequently, `TraitCompiler` leaves `@NgModule(...)` intact and omits `ɵmod`, `ɵinj`, `ɵfac`, and `ɵsetClassMetadata`.

In `ng-analyze`, `optimize_ng_module` previously cleared `declarations`/`imports`/`exports` when `outcome.failed` was `true`, which still emitted an empty `NgModuleMetadata` over the wire in full compilation mode — causing `processor.ts` to strip `@NgModule(...)` (triggering `TS6133` unused-import errors under `noUnusedLocals: true` for symbols only referenced inside `@NgModule`) and emit empty `ɵfac`/`ɵmod`/`ɵinj`/`ɵsetClassMetadata` definitions. Furthermore, on a class co-decorated with `@Injectable() @NgModule(...)`, stripping `@NgModule` or emitting `ɵprov` without `ɵfac` produces broken `.ng.ts` TypeScript output (`TS6133` / `TS2339`).

This change:
1. Adds `analysis_failed: bool` to `NgModuleData` and sets it to `true` in `optimize_ng_module` when `outcome.failed` is `true`.
2. Filters all `DecoratorData::NgModule(m) if m.analysis_failed` classes out of `FileData::to_wire` in full compilation mode (with a `TODO(parity)` comment documenting why co-located `@Injectable()` codegen is also suppressed on `.ng.ts` output, plus a defensive `!m.analysis_failed` guard in `ClassData::to_wire`).
3. Skips downstream `NG6100` (`module.id`) and pure-`@NgModule` `NG2003` constructor dependency diagnostics when `m.analysis_failed` is `true`, while preserving `NG6xxx` scope diagnostics and `strictInjectionParameters` `NG2003` validation when a co-located `@Injectable()` requires a valid constructor.

### Input

```ts
// ext.d.ts
import * as i0 from '@angular/core';
export declare class ExternalComponent {
  static ɵcmp: i0.ɵɵComponentDeclaration<
    ExternalComponent,
    'ext-comp',
    never,
    {},
    {},
    never,
    never,
    false,
    never
  >;
}

// app.ts (compiled with strictInjectionParameters: true, noUnusedLocals: true)
import {Injectable, NgModule} from '@angular/core';
import {ExternalComponent} from './ext';

@NgModule({
  declarations: [ExternalComponent],
})
export class BrokenModule {
  constructor(dep: unknown) {}
}

@Injectable()
@NgModule({
  declarations: [ExternalComponent],
})
export class BrokenInjectableModule {
  constructor(dep: unknown) {}
}
```

### Output Before Fix (`ngp`)

Reports `NG6001` (x2) and spurious `NG2003` on `BrokenModule`, strips `@NgModule` (causing `TS6133: 'ExternalComponent' is declared but its value is never read`), and emits broken static definitions.

### Output After Fix (`ngp`)

Reports `NG6001` on both modules and `NG2003` only on `BrokenInjectableModule`, leaves both classes and their decorators untouched in `.ng.ts` (zero `TS6133`/`TS2339` errors), and continues compiling valid sibling classes normally:
```ts
@NgModule({
  declarations: [ExternalComponent],
})
export class BrokenModule {
  constructor(dep: unknown) {}
}

@Injectable()
@NgModule({
  declarations: [ExternalComponent],
})
export class BrokenInjectableModule {
  constructor(dep: unknown) {}
}
```

In `ngtsc`, an unbound identifier in Angular decorator metadata resolves through TypeScript's global scope like any other value. An example is Closure's `COMPILED`, declared by `declare var COMPILED: boolean;` in a `.d.ts` file listed in `tsconfig.json` `files`. `ng-analyze` only indexed the `declare module` blocks in those files, so it treated these identifiers as unknown. In full compilation it fell back to emitting the unevaluated expression into `ɵɵsetNgModuleScope` and typed `ɵmod` as the class itself. Fields that must be static, such as `selector`, reported `NG1010` (`NG11001` in local compilation).

This change indexes the ambient global values declared in the tsconfig's `.d.ts` files (top-level declarations in script `.d.ts` files, and `declare global` blocks). It resolves unbound value identifiers against them in full, `experimental-local`, and `emitDeclarationOnly` compilation, evaluating the declaration as `ngtsc` does: `declare var COMPILED: boolean` is a reference, and `declare const ENV: 'prod'` is `'prod'`. Identifiers that no `.d.ts` declares as a value still report `NG1010`/`NG11001`.

Follow-ups, stacked on this PR:
- #71850: `hostDirectives` no longer drops entries in local compilation, and folds ambient globals there.
- #71851: editing a `.d.ts` only re-analyzes the files whose global lookups it changes.

### Input

```ts
// closure.lib.d.ts (listed in tsconfig.json "files")
declare var COMPILED: boolean;

// store.module.ts
import {NgModule} from '@angular/core';
import {MocksModule} from './mocks';

@NgModule({})
export class StoreDepsModule {}

@NgModule({
  imports: [StoreDepsModule, ...(COMPILED ? [MocksModule] : [])],
})
export class StoreModule {}
```

### Output Before Fix (`ngp`)

```ts
export class StoreModule {
  static ɵmod: StoreModule = /*@__PURE__*/ i0.ɵɵdefineNgModule({type: StoreModule});
  static ɵinj: i0.ɵɵInjectorDeclaration<StoreModule> = /*@__PURE__*/ i0.ɵɵdefineInjector({
    imports: [StoreDepsModule, ...(COMPILED ? [MocksModule] : [])],
  });
  // ...
}
(function () {
  (typeof ngJitMode === 'undefined' || ngJitMode) &&
    i0.ɵɵsetNgModuleScope(StoreModule, {
      imports: [StoreDepsModule, ...(COMPILED ? [MocksModule] : [])],
    });
})();
```

### Output After Fix (`ngp` — matches `ngtsc`)

```ts
export class StoreModule {
  static ɵmod: i0.ɵɵNgModuleDeclaration<
    StoreModule,
    never,
    [typeof StoreDepsModule, typeof MocksModule],
    never
  > = /*@__PURE__*/ i0.ɵɵdefineNgModule({type: StoreModule});
  static ɵinj: i0.ɵɵInjectorDeclaration<StoreModule> = /*@__PURE__*/ i0.ɵɵdefineInjector({
    imports: [StoreDepsModule, (COMPILED ? [MocksModule] : [])],
  });
  // ...
}
(function () {
  (typeof ngJitMode === 'undefined' || ngJitMode) &&
    i0.ɵɵsetNgModuleScope(StoreModule, {imports: [StoreDepsModule, MocksModule]});
})();
```

